'''''Spidey and His Amazing Friends''''', also known as '''''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends''''', is a preschool animated television series produced by [[Marvel Studios Animation]] (formerly [[Marvel Animation]]) and animated by [[Atomic Cartoons]] (who also produced ''[[Marvel Super Hero Adventures]]''), which premiered on [[Disney Jr.]] on August 6, 2021. The show features young versions of the Marvel characters and is the first full-length Marvel animated series targeted at young audiences.

The series has been consistently renewed for additional seasons prior to their premieres. On August 15, 2026, the show was renewed for a seventh season.<ref name="Season 7 Renewal & Halloween special">{{Cite web |last1=Jackson |first1=Destiny |last2=Garner |first2=Glenn |date=August 15, 2026 |title=All Things Spidey At D23: Tom Holland, Anniversary Comic Book, ''Friendly Neighborhood'' Sneak-Peak, ''Amazing Friends'' Renewal & Upcoming Special ''Spidey and the Avengers: Halloween Team-Up!'' |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/all-things-spidey-d23-friendly-neighborhood-amazing-friends-1237040751/ |access-date=August 15, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>

A [[Spin-off (media)|spin-off]] series, ''[[Iron Man and His Awesome Friends]]'', premiered on August 11, 2025. Three days before its premiere, another upcoming spin-off, ''Avengers: Mightiest Friends'', was announced in August 2025 and is slated to premiere in 2027.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2025-08-07 |title=Disney Jr. is expanding its preschool universe with 'Marvel's Avengers: Mightiest Friends' |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/tv/story/2025-08-07/avengers-mightiest-friends-marvel-disney-jr |access-date=2026-04-24 |website=Los Angeles Times |language=en-US}}</ref>

==Plot==
The series follows the adventures of grade school kid incarnations of [[Spider-Man|Peter Parker / Spidey]],  [[Spider-Woman (Gwen Stacy)|Gwen Stacy / Ghost-Spider]], and [[Miles Morales|Miles Morales / Spin]] and as they fight villains across [[New York City]] such as [[Rhino (character)|Rhino]],<ref name="dcb0" /> [[Lady Octopus|Doc Ock]], her Octobot partner CAL, her Octobots, [[Green Goblin]], [[Electro (Marvel Comics)#Francine Frye|Electro]], [[Black Cat (Marvel Comics)|Black Cat]], [[Sandman (Marvel Comics)|Sandman]], [[Arnim Zola|Zola]], his Hydrabots, [[Lizard (character)|Lizard]], [[Trapster]], [[Hydro-Man]], [[Symbie]], and [[Swarm (Marvel Comics)|Swarm]].

Spidey, Spin, and Ghost-Spider would sometimes receive aid from other superheroes such as [[Black Panther (character)|Black Panther]], [[Kamala Khan|Ms. Marvel]], her dog [[Lockjaw (character)|Lockjaw]], [[Hulk]], [[Iron Man]], [[Ant-Man]], [[Wasp (character)|Wasp]], [[Reptil]], [[Thing (Marvel Comics)|Thing]], his partners [[H.E.R.B.I.E.]] and [[Mr. Fantastic]], [[Squirrel Girl]], her sidekick [[Tippy-Toe]], [[White Tiger (Ava Ayala)|White Tiger]], [[Captain America]], [[Jeff the Land Shark]], [[Rocket Raccoon]], his partner [[Groot]], and [[Silk (character)|Silk]].

