==Production==
===Development===
[[Marvel Animation]] announced its first preschool series ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' in August 2019.<ref name="dcb0">{{Cite press release |title=Marvel Animation Announces Its First Full-Length Preschool Series "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" |date=August 23, 2019 |publisher=[[Disney Channel]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2019/08/23/marvel-animation-announces-its-first-full-length-preschool-series-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-832310/20190823disney11/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=May 14, 2021}}</ref> Disney Jr. renewed the series for a second season in August 2021.<ref name="S2Renewal">{{Cite web |last=Del Rosario |first=Alexandra |date=August 18, 2021 |title=''Marvel's Spidey And His Amazing Friends'' Renewed For Season 2 By Disney Junior |url=https://deadline.com/2021/08/marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-renewed-season-2-disney-junior-1234814334/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210905104554/https://deadline.com/2021/08/marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-renewed-season-2-disney-junior-1234814334/ |archive-date=September 5, 2021 |access-date=August 18, 2021 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> On June 15, 2022, Disney Jr. renewed the series for a third season.<ref name="S3Renewal">{{Cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Lise |date=June 15, 2022 |title=Disney Reveals Animated Series Slate at Annecy Festival (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/disney-annecy-1235294867/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220712065759/https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/disney-annecy-1235294867/ |archive-date=July 12, 2022 |access-date=June 15, 2022 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> [[Marvel Studios Animation]] took over production of the series starting with season 2.<ref name="Season 2 News" /> Disney Jr. further renewed the series for a fourth season on June 13, 2023,<ref name="S4Renewal">{{Cite web |last=Bałaga |first=Marta |date=June 13, 2023 |title=Disney Unveils Animated Series at Annecy, Teases ''Magicampers'' and ''The Sunnyridge 3'' (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2023/tv/global/magicampers-the-sunnyridge-3-disney-1235642369/ |access-date=June 13, 2023 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-date=June 13, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230613164835/https://variety.com/2023/tv/global/magicampers-the-sunnyridge-3-disney-1235642369/ |url-status=live }}</ref> a fifth season on February 27, 2025,<ref name="Season 5 Renewal">{{Cite press release |title=Disney Jr.'s "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" Renewed for a Fifth Season |date=February 27, 2025 |publisher=[[Disney Branded Television]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2025/02/27/disney-jrs-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-renewed-for-a-fifth-season-29215/20250227disney01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref> a sixth season five months later on June 7,<ref name="Season 6 Renewal">{{Cite web |last=Lang |first=Jamie |date=June 7, 2025 |title=''Spidey and his Amazing Friends'', ''Dragon Striker'' and ''Sam Witch'' Headline Disney Branded TV's Annecy Slate (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/global/disney-branded-tv-annecy-slate-1236422042/ |access-date=June 7, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> and a seventh season during the ''Celebrate 65 Years of Marvel's Spider-Man!'' panel at [[D23 (Disney)|D23: The Ultimate Disney Fan Event]] in [[Anaheim, California]] on August 15, 2026.<ref name="Season 7 Renewal & Halloween special" /> 

With its preemptive sixth and seventh season renewals, ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' is slated to jointly become Disney Jr. and Marvel's longest running animated series by episode count, surpassing ''[[Doc McStuffins]]'' (136 episodes) and [[Disney XD]]'s ''[[Avengers Assemble (TV series)|Avengers Assemble]]'' (127 episodes) with five seasons each. It is also the second Marvel television series overall to be renewed for seven seasons after [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]]'s ''[[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.]]'', as well as the second series within any of Disney's core branded networks (and the first for both its animated catalog and Disney Jr.) to reach this milestone after [[Disney Channel]]'s ''[[Bunk'd]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Chitwood |first=Adam |date=January 9, 2026 |title=How Disney Kids Sensation ''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' Reached 1 Billion Hours Streamed in 100 Episodes |url=https://www.thewrap.com/creative-content/tv-shows/spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-100th-episode-symbiote/ |access-date=June 1, 2026 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref>

===Music===
[[Patrick Stump]] of the pop punk rock band [[Fall Out Boy]] wrote, composed, and performed the theme song for the series.<ref name="Music">{{Cite press release |title=Grammy(R) Award-Nominated Musician Patrick Stump Performs Theme Song for "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends", Premiering This Summer on Disney Junior |date=June 8, 2021 |publisher=[[Disney Channel]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2021/06/08/grammy-award-nominated-musician-patrick-stump-performs-theme-song-for-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-premiering-this-summer-on-disney-junior--114511/20210608disney01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=August 7, 2021}}</ref> A longtime Marvel fan, he used themes from previous ''Spider-Man'' media as inspiration.<ref>[https://ew.com/tv/patrick-stump-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-theme-song/ Patrick Stump breaks down his theme song for new cartoon ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends''] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210608000150/https://ew.com/tv/patrick-stump-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-theme-song/ |date=June 8, 2021 }} ''Entertainment Weekly'' June 7, 2021</ref>

The first 68 episodes also used an instrumental for the opening theme, but for episode 69 onwards, the ending theme is "Do the Spidey", which was written by Stump and series story writer Harrison Willcox, and performed by Stump.<ref>{{cite web |last=Barilla |first=Chris |title=Fall Out Boy's Patrick Stump Teases His ''Amazing'' New Music, Dropping Today |url=https://people.com/patrick-stump-writing-music-for-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-exclusive-8663139 |access-date=August 15, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |date=June 14, 2024}}</ref><ref name="Go Dino-Webs Go! / Ghost in the Museum"/>

==Release==
''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' premiered with a series of 11 short episodes titled ''Meet Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' on June 21, 2021, on [[Disney Channel]] and Disney Jr.,<ref name="Premiere Date">{{Cite press release |title="Jump Into Wow" This Summer on Disney Junior with "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" and "Mickey Mouse Funhouse" |date=June 16, 2021 |publisher=[[Disney Channel]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2021/06/16/jump-into-wow-this-summer-on-disney-junior-with-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-and-mickey-mouse-funhouse-725113/20210616disney01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=June 16, 2021 |archive-date=November 29, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231129185546/http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2021/06/16/jump-into-wow-this-summer-on-disney-junior-with-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-and-mickey-mouse-funhouse-725113/20210616disney01/ |url-status=live }}</ref> followed by [[Disney+]] on July 16.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bjornson |first=Greta |date=June 16, 2021 |title=New on Disney+ July 2021 |url=https://decider.com/2021/06/16/new-on-disney-plus-july-2021/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210703044042/https://decider.com/2021/06/16/new-on-disney-plus-july-2021/ |archive-date=July 3, 2021 |access-date=August 7, 2021 |website=[[New York Post#Website|Decider]] |publisher=[[New York Post]]}}</ref> The series also premiered on September 11, 2021, in Southeast Asia, but only lasted 20 days before the channel's closure on October 1, 2021.{{citation needed|date=March 2022}}

The full series premiered on August 6 with a simulcast on Disney Jr. and Disney Channel,<ref name="Premiere Date" /> later on Disney+ on September 22.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Peters |first=Fletcher |date=August 17, 2021 |title=New on Disney+ September 2021 |url=https://decider.com/2021/08/17/new-on-disney-plus-september-2021/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210901220714/https://decider.com/2021/08/17/new-on-disney-plus-september-2021/ |archive-date=September 1, 2021 |access-date=August 18, 2021 |website=[[New York Post#Website|Decider]] |publisher=[[New York Post]]}}</ref>

The second season of ''Meet Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' premiered on July 18, 2022, on Disney Channel and Disney Jr., followed by Disney+ on August 17.<ref name="Season 2 Premiere Date">{{Cite press release |title=Second Season of Disney Branded Television's Web-Slinging Preschool Series "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" Premieres Friday, Aug. 19 |date=July 15, 2022 |publisher=[[Disney Branded Television]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2022/07/15/second-season-of-disney-branded-televisions-web-slinging-preschool-series-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-premieres-friday-aug-19-223211/20220715disney01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=July 15, 2022 |archive-date=September 24, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230924124847/http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2022/07/15/second-season-of-disney-branded-televisions-web-slinging-preschool-series-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-premieres-friday-aug-19-223211/20220715disney01/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The second season of the series premiered on August 19, 2022, with a simulcast on Disney Jr. and Disney Channel, followed by Disney+ later on.<ref name="Season 2 News">{{Cite press release |title=Alice! Mickey! Pooh! Spidey! Disney Junior Announces Slate of New Original Series and Shorts, Along With Returning Franchises, Debuting Across Disney+ and Disney Junior Platforms Through 2024 at First-Ever Disney Junior Fun Fest |date=April 29, 2022 |publisher=[[Disney Branded Television]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2022/04/29/alice-mickey-pooh-spidey-disney-junior-announces-slate-of-new-original-series-and-shorts-along-with-returning-franchises-debuting-across-disneyplus-and-disney-junior-platforms-through-2024-at-first-ever-disney-junior-fun-fest-354415/20220429disney02/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=April 29, 2022 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20230323230352/http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2022/04/29/alice-mickey-pooh-spidey-disney-junior-announces-slate-of-new-original-series-and-shorts-along-with-returning-franchises-debuting-across-disneyplus-and-disney-junior-platforms-through-2024-at-first-ever-disney-junior-fun-fest-354415/20220429disney02/ |archive-date=March 23, 2023}}</ref><ref name="Season 2 Premiere Date" />

On October 10, 2022, the series debuted on [[CBeebies]] in the United Kingdom, making this the first show based on a Disney property to premiere on said network.<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 10, 2021 |title=''Marvel's Spidey and his Amazing Friends'': Hulk Needs Team Spidey's Help |url=https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/spidey-his-amazing-friends-camping-conundrum-great-green-crime-spree |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221002130552/https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/spidey-his-amazing-friends-camping-conundrum-great-green-crime-spree |archive-date=October 2, 2022 |access-date=September 30, 2022 |website=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref>

The third season of the series premiered on January 8, 2024, on Disney Channel and Disney Jr., followed by Disney+ later on.<ref name="Season 3 Premiere Date">{{Cite web |date=December 5, 2023 |title=''Spidey and his Amazing Friends'' Swings Back for Season 3 |url=https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-season-3 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231205202611/https://www.marvel.com/articles/tv-shows/spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-season-3 |archive-date=December 5, 2023 |website=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref> A [[Crossover (fiction)|crossover]] episode with ''[[Moon Girl and Devil Dinosaur]]'', "[[List of Spidey and His Amazing Friends episodes#ep79|Moon Girl and the Dino Dilemma]]", aired on November 15, 2024.<ref name="Moon Girl Crossover"/>

The fourth season of the series premiered on June 16, 2025 on Disney Jr., followed by Disney+ on June 17.<ref name="Season 4 Premiere Date">{{Cite press release |title="Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" Season Four Premieres June 16 on Disney Jr. and Next Day on Disney+ |date=May 29, 2025 |publisher=[[Disney Branded Television]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2025/05/29/marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-season-four-premieres-june-16-on-disney-jr-and-next-day-on-disneyplus-24012/20250529disney01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref>

The fifth season of the series premiered on July 13, 2026 on Disney Jr., followed by Disney+ on July 14.<ref name="Season 5 Premiere Date">{{Cite press release |title=Rocket, Groot, Mr. Fantastic and Silk Join "Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends" Season 5, Premiering July 13 |date=June 8, 2026 |publisher=[[Disney Branded Television]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2026/06/08/rocket-groot-mr-fantastic-and-silk-join-marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-season-5-premiering-july-13-640110/20260608disney02/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref>

=== Spin-offs ===
A [[Spin-off (media)|spin-off]] series, ''[[Iron Man and His Awesome Friends]]'', premiered on Disney Jr. on August 11, 2025, and its first ten episodes premiered on [[Disney+]] the next day. 

''Iron Man and His Awesome Friends'' is set to end after 40 episodes over a single season to make way for the second upcoming spin-off, ''Avengers: Mightiest Friends'', which was announced in August 2025 and is slated to premiere in 2027.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Palmer |first=Roger |date=2026-07-20 |title="Marvel’s Iron Man and his Awesome Friends" To Become "Marvel's Avengers: Mightiest Friends" |url=https://whatsondisneyplus.com/marvels-iron-man-and-his-awesome-friends-to-end-after-one-season/ |access-date=2026-07-22 |website=What's On Disney Plus |language=en-us}}</ref>

=== Marketing ===
A story based on the series was released on May 3, 2025, alongside an ''[[Iron Man and His Awesome Friends]]'' story as part of a [[Free Comic Book Day]] comic.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Marvel Reveals 2025 Free Comic Book Day Titles Starring the Fantastic Four, X-Men, and More |url=https://www.marvel.com/articles/comics/2025-free-comic-book-day-fantastic-four-xmen-spider-man-ironheart |access-date=March 20, 2025 |website=[[Marvel Entertainment]]}}</ref>

== Reception ==
===Critical response===
Adam Levine of ''[[Looper (website)|Looper]]'' ranked ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' 19th in their "Every 2021 Superhero Movie And TV Show Ranked" list, asserting, "Bright, colorful, and wonderfully animated, it doesn't get high marks from comic book diehards, but has been nonetheless well-reviewed by parents of its young target audience for its wholesome stories and message of teamwork."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Levine |first=Adam |date=January 4, 2022 |title=Every 2021 Superhero Movie And TV Show Ranked |url=https://www.looper.com/724621/every-2021-superhero-movie-and-tv-show-ranked/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220907004053/https://www.looper.com/724621/every-2021-superhero-movie-and-tv-show-ranked/ |archive-date=September 7, 2022 |access-date=September 7, 2022 |website=[[Looper (website)|Looper]]}}</ref> Polly Conway of ''[[Common Sense Media]]'' rated the series three out of five stars, writing, "The whole "Marvel Babies" concept may be a little odd for parents, and more cynical viewers might see the show as a way to get even younger kids interested in the vast, lucrative Marvel franchise. But overall the show is charming, well-paced, and a solid choice for younger siblings who aren't ready for the movies or more mature cartoons."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Conway |first=Polly |title=''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' TV Review |url=https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220907004055/https://www.commonsensemedia.org/tv-reviews/marvels-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends |archive-date=September 7, 2022 |access-date=September 7, 2022 |website=[[Common Sense Media]]}}</ref>

Marisa Lascala of ''[[Good Housekeeping]]'' included ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' in their "60 Best Kids' TV Shows and Family Series of All Time" list.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lascala |first=Marisa |date=June 30, 2022 |title=60 Best Kids' TV Shows and Family Series of All Time |url=https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/life/entertainment/g28087907/best-kids-tv-shows/ |access-date=August 14, 2023 |website=[[Good Housekeeping]] |language=en-US |archive-date=August 16, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230816203713/https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/life/entertainment/g28087907/best-kids-tv-shows/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Dakota Mayes of ''[[MovieWeb]]'' ranked ''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' 5th in their "Best Animated Spider-Man Series" list, stating, "''Spider-Man and His Amazing Friends'' is different from all others on this list in that it is geared towards toddlers. This modern update of the classic 80's cartoon left out Iceman and Firestar, and traded them with other popular web-slingers like Ghost-Spider/Gwen Stacy and Miles Morales, nicknamed 'Spin' to avoid confusion with Peter Parker's alter ego. This trio appeared in two computer-animated shorts per episode that were filled with youthful fun and adventures. Each adorably animated episode featured a classic Spider-Man villain committing some mild manner of mischief. More than that, the series even included an occasional appearance from Marvel superheroes like Black Panther and Captain Marvel to add to the age-appropriate fun. This show was such a hit with its targeted age group that it earned itself a second season", which aired in 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mayes |first=Dakota |date=December 14, 2021 |title=Best Animated ''Spider-Man'' Series, Ranked |url=https://movieweb.com/spider-man-animated-series-best/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220907004054/https://movieweb.com/spider-man-animated-series-best/ |archive-date=September 7, 2022 |access-date=September 7, 2022 |website=[[MovieWeb]]}}</ref>

=== Ratings ===
[[Nielsen Media Research]], which records viewership on certain American television screens, reported that ''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' ranked as the second most-watched streaming series among children aged 2–5 during the fourth quarter of 2024. The series also placed No. 2 among boys in the same age group, surpassing other major preschool series like ''[[Paw Patrol]]'' and ''[[Cocomelon]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hailu |first=Selome |date=2025-02-27 |title=''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' Renewed for Season 5 at Disney Jr. After Big Ratings Win (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/marvel-spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-season-5-1236322509/ |access-date=2025-02-28 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US}}</ref> It has garnered over 2 billion views across Disney Jr. and Marvel HQ's YouTube channels, and has accumulated over 1 billion hours watched across linear TV and streaming on Disney+ in the United States.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Milligan |first=Mercedes |date=2025-02-28 |title=''Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' Renewed for 5th Season |url=https://www.animationmagazine.net/2025/02/spidey-and-his-amazing-friends-renewed-for-5th-season/ |access-date=2025-02-28 |website=[[Animation Magazine]] |language=en-US}}</ref> In December 2025, Disney announced that ''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' was among the television series to surpass one billion hours streamed on Disney+ in 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |date=2025-12-17 |title=Disney+ and Hulu: 2025 Year in Streaming |url=https://thewaltdisneycompany.com/2025-streaming-numbers/ |access-date=2025-12-19 |website=[[The Walt Disney Company]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Artavia |first=David |date=December 18, 2025 |title=Disney’s 2025 Streaming Numbers Are In — ‘Bluey’ Is Still on Top With Over 26M Rewatches |url=https://parade.com/news/disney-2025-streaming-numbers-are-in-bluey-is-still-on-top-with-over-26m-rewatches |access-date=December 19, 2025 |website=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]]}}</ref> The series generated 73.7 billion minutes of watch time during the period from January 1, 2023, to July 4, 2026, according to Nielsen.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gruenwedel |first=Erik |date=2026-08-07 |title=Nielsen: Animated 'Spider-Man' Movies, TV Shows Top Theatrical Across U.S. Household TV/Streaming Views |url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/nielsen-animated-spider-man-movies-top-theatrical-across-us-household-tv-streaming-views/ |access-date=2026-09-14 |website=[[Media Play News]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Carter |first=Justin |date=2026-08-23 |title=Daaaaaaaamn, People Love Watching Spider-Man Movies |url=https://gizmodo.com/daaaaaaaamn-people-love-watching-spider-man-movies-2000801957 |access-date=2026-09-14 |website=[[Gizmodo]] |language=en-US}}</ref> ''Marvel's Spidey and His Amazing Friends'' accumulated 20.7 billion minutes of viewing across linear television and streaming platforms between September 22, 2025, and September 20, 2026, ranking as the tenth most-watched animated series during that period.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 2026 |title=Drawn to Watch: Animation’s Hit Makers |url=https://www.nielsen.com/insights/2026/drawn-to-watch-animations-hit-makers/ |access-date=2026-11-06 |website=[[Nielsen Media Research]] |publisher=[[Nielsen Holdings]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2026-10-27 |title=Nielsen Animation Day 2026 Reports Highlights Key Toon TV & Streaming Trends |url=https://www.animationmagazine.net/2026/10/nielsen-animation-day-2026-reports-highlights-key-toon-tv-streaming-trends/ |access-date=2026-11-06 |website=[[Animation Magazine]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

=== Accolades ===
The series was nominated for Best Editing in an Animated Pre-School Series at the 2023 [[Canadian Cinema Editors Awards]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=MacRae |first=Jane |date=December 4, 2022 |title=13th Annual CCE Awards » Canadian Cinema Editors / Les Monteurs et Monteuses de cinéma canadien |url=https://cceditors.ca/2022/12/04/13th-annual-cce-awards/ |access-date=May 23, 2023 |website=[[Canadian Cinema Editors]] |language=en-CA |archive-date=May 31, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230531194726/https://cceditors.ca/2022/12/04/13th-annual-cce-awards/ |url-status=live }}</ref> It was also nominated for [[NAACP Image Award for Outstanding Animated Series|Outstanding Animated Series]] at the [[55th NAACP Image Awards]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hipes |first=Patrick |date=January 25, 2024 |title=Colman Domingo, Keke Palmer, Ayo Edebiri, Victoria Monét Lead NAACP Image Awards Nominations |url=https://deadline.com/2024/01/2024-naacp-image-awards-nominations-list-1235804254/ |access-date=January 28, 2024 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>

